1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,380
Four thousand dollars off a Toyota HiLux.

2
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:06,450
CarsGuide called it a "rare" move
because Toyota almost never needs to

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,730
discount Australia's most famous ute.

4
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:12,510
But in October 2026, that's
exactly what happened.

5
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,850
And Toyota isn't alone.

6
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,910
Ford has cut its Ranger plug-in hybrid
by more than ten thousand dollars and

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:20,730
handed out four-thousand-dollar
fuel cards.

8
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:24,050
Kia has slashed up to fifteen
thousand dollars off its Tasman.

9
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:28,170
BYD is offering four thousand
dollars cashback on the Shark 6.

10
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:30,570
Australia's ute market
the most profitable,

11
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:34,170
most fiercely defended part of the whole
car industry is in a full-blown price

12
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:34,870
war.

13
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:35,830
Why now?

14
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:39,870
Because Australians are buying fewer
traditional utes and the brands know it.

15
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:43,410
Sales of traditional utes and vans were
down more than thirteen per cent in

16
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:46,470
September, and down more than
ten per cent for the year.

17
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:49,357
Some of the biggest names are
going backwards by thirty,

18
00:00:49,407 --> 00:00:50,890
forty, even fifty per cent.

19
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:54,910
In this video, I'll show you who's
cutting prices, by how much, and why.

20
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:58,430
I'll show you which utes are winning
and which are getting crushed.

21
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,110
And at the end,

22
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,510
I'll tell you how to get the best
possible deal and the traps hidden inside

23
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,680
some of these offers.

24
00:01:04,395 --> 00:01:05,525
Let's start with the numbers,

25
00:01:05,575 --> 00:01:08,605
because they're the reason
all of this is happening.

26
00:01:08,655 --> 00:01:09,735
In September 2026,

27
00:01:09,785 --> 00:01:13,185
the Ford Ranger was Australia's
best-selling vehicle,

28
00:01:13,235 --> 00:01:16,445
with 5,062 sales, up four per cent.

29
00:01:16,495 --> 00:01:23,085
But the Toyota HiLux fell to fourth,
with 4,455 down 11.7 per cent.

30
00:01:23,135 --> 00:01:26,205
Even more telling, the Toyota RAV4 SUV,

31
00:01:26,255 --> 00:01:30,065
with 4,624 sales, outsold the HiLux.

32
00:01:30,115 --> 00:01:32,085
Not long ago, that would
have been unthinkable.

33
00:01:32,135 --> 00:01:33,295
For the year to date,

34
00:01:33,345 --> 00:01:36,565
the race for Australia's number
one vehicle is incredibly tight.

35
00:01:36,615 --> 00:01:40,545
The Ranger is on 37,858.

36
00:01:40,595 --> 00:01:44,065
The HiLux is on 36,616.

37
00:01:44,115 --> 00:01:47,805
That's a gap of just over twelve
hundred, with three months to go.

38
00:01:47,855 --> 00:01:50,825
And winning that crown matters
enormously for marketing,

39
00:01:50,875 --> 00:01:52,365
for dealers and for pride.

40
00:01:52,415 --> 00:01:54,625
Back in May, CarsGuide's news editor,

41
00:01:54,675 --> 00:01:56,545
Dom Tripolone, put it bluntly:

42
00:01:56,595 --> 00:02:00,805
"We've hit peak ute and the only way is
down." Four-wheel-drive ute sales were

43
00:02:00,855 --> 00:02:04,005
already falling then, and
the decline has continued.

44
00:02:04,055 --> 00:02:05,505
It's a remarkable turnaround.

45
00:02:05,555 --> 00:02:07,085
For most of the past decade,

46
00:02:07,135 --> 00:02:11,105
the Ranger and the HiLux took turns
as the country's best-selling vehicle.

47
00:02:11,155 --> 00:02:13,105
Toyota's former sales and marketing boss,

48
00:02:13,155 --> 00:02:16,605
Sean Hanley, saw this coming
back at the start of 2025.

49
00:02:16,655 --> 00:02:20,485
He said "the number of ute models
available to Australian buyers will expand

50
00:02:20,535 --> 00:02:24,405
rapidly", and that an SUV could rise
to the top of the national sales charts

51
00:02:24,455 --> 00:02:26,185
"in the next year or two".

52
00:02:26,235 --> 00:02:27,345
He was right on both counts.

53
00:02:27,395 --> 00:02:29,645
So what's driving buyers away?

54
00:02:29,695 --> 00:02:30,905
Three big things.

55
00:02:30,955 --> 00:02:32,125
First, fuel.

56
00:02:32,175 --> 00:02:33,785
In May 2026,

57
00:02:33,835 --> 00:02:38,045
diesel reached as high as $3.50 a
litre in some parts of Australia,

58
00:02:38,095 --> 00:02:39,325
according to CarExpert.

59
00:02:39,375 --> 00:02:44,045
Fill an eighty-litre ute tank at that
price and you're up for about $280.

60
00:02:44,095 --> 00:02:46,405
Second, the government's emissions rules.

61
00:02:46,455 --> 00:02:48,058
Under the New Vehicle Efficiency Standard,

62
00:02:48,108 --> 00:02:52,105
car makers face penalties for selling
too many high-emitting vehicles and

63
00:02:52,155 --> 00:02:54,915
diesel utes are some of the
highest emitters on the market.

64
00:02:54,965 --> 00:02:56,985
Third, the alternatives have exploded.

65
00:02:57,035 --> 00:02:59,665
Plug-in hybrid utes, Chinese utes,

66
00:02:59,715 --> 00:03:02,445
and family SUVs with
hybrid and electric power.

67
00:03:02,495 --> 00:03:06,245
Chinese-built vehicles made up more
than thirty-five per cent of all new-car

68
00:03:06,295 --> 00:03:07,885
sales in September.

69
00:03:07,935 --> 00:03:11,575
Buyers who once defaulted to a dual-cab
now have a dozen other options.

70
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:15,620
So let's look at the deals,
starting with the big one: Toyota.

71
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:22,050
Toyota is offering a $4,000 "deposit
bonus" on new and demonstrator 2026

72
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:25,700
HiLux SR5 models the
four-wheel-drive versions.

73
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:32,050
CarsGuide reported that the SR5
range starts at $69,901 drive-away

74
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:33,570
in New South Wales,

75
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:40,077
rising to $73,952 for the top
double-cab cab-chassis with the new

76
00:03:40,127 --> 00:03:41,670
48-volt mild-hybrid system.

77
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,180
But read the fine print.

78
00:03:43,230 --> 00:03:47,370
The bonus only applies if you finance
the ute through Toyota Finance,

79
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,650
with at least ten
thousand dollars borrowed.

80
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:53,750
Finance applications have to be in
between the 1st of September and the 31st

81
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:59,730
of December 2026, and the car has to be
settled by the 28th of February 2027.

82
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:02,610
It covers private buyers and
some smaller fleet customers,

83
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,810
and it excludes the electric HiLux.

84
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:06,430
Why is Toyota doing this?

85
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,150
Its sales boss, John Pappas,

86
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:10,350
said Toyota is "targeting a very strong,

87
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:14,990
record fourth quarter sales for 2026,"
thanks to better vehicle supply.

88
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:17,710
In plain English: Toyota
has more utes coming,

89
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,790
it wants to move them,

90
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:21,570
and it wants to stop the Ranger
from running away with the title.

91
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,830
And remember, this is a brand-new HiLux.

92
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:26,250
The new generation arrived in late 2025,

93
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:30,170
with a mild-hybrid diesel and
even a fully electric version.

94
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:33,170
Normally, a new model sells
strongly in its first year.

95
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:36,570
Instead, the HiLux was down almost
twelve per cent in September.

96
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:38,430
Toyota needs this one to work.

97
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,370
That's worth remembering.

98
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:43,310
When the market leader starts offering
finance bonuses on its most iconic

99
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:45,360
model, it's not doing it for fun.

100
00:04:47,505 --> 00:04:47,541
Now Ford.

101
00:04:47,591 --> 00:04:52,581
Ford's Ranger has been Australia's
best-selling vehicle in 2024 and 2025,

102
00:04:52,631 --> 00:04:55,121
and it's leading again in 2026.

103
00:04:55,171 --> 00:04:57,581
But even the champion
has been cutting prices.

104
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:59,301
In April 2026,

105
00:04:59,351 --> 00:05:03,101
Ford slashed the price of the Ranger
plug-in hybrid now simply called the

106
00:05:03,151 --> 00:05:04,301
Ranger Hybrid.

107
00:05:04,351 --> 00:05:07,921
The XLT Hybrid dropped
to $62,000 drive-away.

108
00:05:07,971 --> 00:05:12,881
It had been listed at
$71,990 before on-road costs,

109
00:05:12,931 --> 00:05:16,191
so Ford described that as over
ten thousand dollars less.

110
00:05:16,241 --> 00:05:19,401
The Sport was $66,000 drive-away,

111
00:05:19,451 --> 00:05:24,501
the Wildtrak $70,000, and
the Stormtrak $73,000.

112
00:05:24,551 --> 00:05:25,761
At the same time,

113
00:05:25,811 --> 00:05:30,821
Ford handed out a $4,000 fuel card
on 2026-model Rangers and entry-level

114
00:05:30,871 --> 00:05:34,901
Everests, timed with the federal
government's cut to fuel excise.

115
00:05:34,951 --> 00:05:37,041
Ford's Australian boss, Fadi Mawal,

116
00:05:37,091 --> 00:05:40,201
said the offers were about helping
customers through "short-term pain at the

117
00:05:40,251 --> 00:05:40,401
pump".

118
00:05:40,451 --> 00:05:45,081
Farmers registered as primary producers
got an extra thousand dollars off any

119
00:05:45,131 --> 00:05:48,281
Ranger, including the hybrid
and the big Super Duty.

120
00:05:48,331 --> 00:05:49,681
And buyers responded.

121
00:05:49,731 --> 00:05:52,906
After the Wildtrak hybrid
dropped to $70,000 drive-away,

122
00:05:52,956 --> 00:05:56,421
Ford said dealer stock was
soon "all but exhausted".

123
00:05:56,471 --> 00:05:58,201
As a Ford spokesperson put it:

124
00:05:58,251 --> 00:06:01,901
"Australian buyers are doing the maths."
That's the key lesson of this whole

125
00:06:01,951 --> 00:06:02,761
price war.

126
00:06:02,811 --> 00:06:06,821
Cut the price far enough, and buyers
come back even in a falling market.

127
00:06:06,871 --> 00:06:07,821
Here's the interesting part.

128
00:06:07,871 --> 00:06:10,601
Ford is discounting from
a position of strength.

129
00:06:10,651 --> 00:06:12,281
The Ranger is still growing.

130
00:06:12,331 --> 00:06:15,801
Ford isn't panicking about the Ranger
itself it's making sure that when Toyota

131
00:06:15,851 --> 00:06:18,151
finally swings back, there's no opening.

132
00:06:18,999 --> 00:06:22,309
And then there's the ute that's
really struggling: the Kia Tasman.

133
00:06:22,359 --> 00:06:24,299
When Kia launched the Tasman in 2025,

134
00:06:24,349 --> 00:06:28,449
it was the most important new
ute in years Kia's first ever,

135
00:06:28,499 --> 00:06:30,409
designed with Australia in mind.

136
00:06:30,459 --> 00:06:33,569
Kia forecast 20,000 sales
in its first calendar year,

137
00:06:33,619 --> 00:06:35,549
and seven to ten per cent of the segment.

138
00:06:35,599 --> 00:06:38,569
It also expected half of
those sales to go to fleets.

139
00:06:38,619 --> 00:06:42,449
Instead, Kia says the split is roughly
one quarter fleet and three quarters

140
00:06:42,499 --> 00:06:46,269
private buyers so the big company orders
it was counting on haven't arrived.

141
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:47,369
The reality?

142
00:06:47,419 --> 00:06:53,789
From launch to the end of September
2026, Kia sold 7,898 Tasmans in total.

143
00:06:53,839 --> 00:06:59,049
In September, it found 355 buyers down
56 per cent on the same month last

144
00:06:59,099 --> 00:06:59,509
year.

145
00:06:59,559 --> 00:07:01,349
So Kia went hard on price.

146
00:07:01,399 --> 00:07:05,209
In May 2026, it cut the
Tasman by up to $15,000.

147
00:07:05,259 --> 00:07:09,449
The top X-Pro dropped
to $64,990 drive-away.

148
00:07:09,499 --> 00:07:13,229
The X-Line came down to $59,990,

149
00:07:13,279 --> 00:07:18,029
and the dual-cab S 4x4 to $49,990.

150
00:07:18,079 --> 00:07:20,382
Kia's own executives have
been remarkably honest.

151
00:07:20,432 --> 00:07:24,549
Then-boss Damien Meredith said
the exterior is "very polarising".

152
00:07:24,599 --> 00:07:26,389
He admitted: "We've fallen short.

153
00:07:26,439 --> 00:07:28,649
We know the facts." But he also said,

154
00:07:28,699 --> 00:07:29,609
"once you're inside it,

155
00:07:29,659 --> 00:07:33,629
it's fantastic." Meredith also pointed
out that the Tasman was planned six

156
00:07:33,679 --> 00:07:36,429
years ago, and the competition
since then has become,

157
00:07:36,479 --> 00:07:37,869
in his words, "quite dramatic".

158
00:07:37,919 --> 00:07:39,689
And at the end of October,

159
00:07:39,739 --> 00:07:41,689
Kia's new chief executive, Dennis Piccoli,

160
00:07:41,739 --> 00:07:44,609
said Kia can do a "vastly
better job" selling the Tasman,

161
00:07:44,659 --> 00:07:46,709
adding: "We'd like to sell more cars.

162
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:47,999
It's as simple as that."

163
00:07:48,715 --> 00:07:51,785
Quick favour before we get to the utes
that are getting crushed and the ones

164
00:07:51,835 --> 00:07:52,885
that are quietly winning.

165
00:07:52,935 --> 00:07:55,085
Are you driving a ute right now?

166
00:07:55,135 --> 00:07:58,425
Would you buy one again with
diesel prices and these discounts?

167
00:07:58,475 --> 00:07:59,765
Tell me in the comments.

168
00:07:59,815 --> 00:08:00,775
And if you want honest,

169
00:08:00,825 --> 00:08:04,405
data-first videos about what's
really happening in Aussie car yards,

170
00:08:04,455 --> 00:08:05,405
hit subscribe.

171
00:08:05,455 --> 00:08:07,615
It's free and it really helps the channel.

172
00:08:09,652 --> 00:08:09,706
Now the scoreboard.

173
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:13,846
Here's how the rest of the ute
market performed in September 2026,

174
00:08:13,896 --> 00:08:17,426
according to VFACTS data published
through CarExpert's sales database.

175
00:08:17,476 --> 00:08:18,866
The losers first.

176
00:08:18,916 --> 00:08:24,106
The Mitsubishi Triton: 1,202
sales, down 30.6 per cent.

177
00:08:24,156 --> 00:08:29,066
The GWM Cannon: 852, down 31.6.

178
00:08:29,116 --> 00:08:33,726
The Mazda BT-50: 843, down 22.5.

179
00:08:33,776 --> 00:08:38,066
The Nissan Navara: 338, down almost 35.

180
00:08:38,116 --> 00:08:42,646
The Volkswagen Amarok:
244, down almost 43.

181
00:08:42,696 --> 00:08:45,806
The KGM Musso: 85, down 38.

182
00:08:45,856 --> 00:08:50,126
And the JAC T9 Chinese
ute: 58, down 47 per cent.

183
00:08:50,176 --> 00:08:51,966
Even the Isuzu D-Max,

184
00:08:52,016 --> 00:08:55,562
one of the most trusted names in
the bush, was down six per cent.

185
00:08:55,612 --> 00:08:57,746
Isuzu is in a particularly tough spot,

186
00:08:57,796 --> 00:08:59,826
because its whole local range is diesel.

187
00:08:59,876 --> 00:09:04,126
In 2026, it cancelled plans to bring
the electric D-Max to Australia,

188
00:09:04,176 --> 00:09:06,586
with Isuzu's Rod Caldwell saying simply:

189
00:09:06,636 --> 00:09:08,776
"Customers don't want
it." Now the winners.

190
00:09:08,826 --> 00:09:11,906
The BYD Shark 6 plug-in hybrid:

191
00:09:11,956 --> 00:09:18,226
1,492 sales, up 25 per cent, and
more than 13,500 for the year.

192
00:09:18,276 --> 00:09:21,626
LDV's cheaper T60: up almost 69 per cent.

193
00:09:21,676 --> 00:09:25,466
LDV's new Terron 9: up 195 per cent.

194
00:09:25,516 --> 00:09:28,706
The Shark 6 is a turnaround
story of its own.

195
00:09:28,756 --> 00:09:33,006
Sales stalled in early 2026
at around 1,200 a month,

196
00:09:33,056 --> 00:09:36,086
after plug-in hybrids lost their
fringe benefits tax exemption.

197
00:09:36,136 --> 00:09:39,006
BYD's chief operating
officer in Australia,

198
00:09:39,056 --> 00:09:40,966
Stephen Collins, admitted at the time:

199
00:09:41,016 --> 00:09:43,486
"I reckon we can do better." By September,

200
00:09:43,536 --> 00:09:46,666
Shark sales were back up twenty-five
per cent on a year earlier.

201
00:09:46,716 --> 00:09:49,006
And big American pick-up trucks the Ram,

202
00:09:49,056 --> 00:09:54,273
Silverado, F-150 and Tundra were up 13
per cent in September and almost 12 per

203
00:09:54,323 --> 00:09:55,506
cent for the year.

204
00:09:55,556 --> 00:09:57,526
So the ute market isn't just shrinking.

205
00:09:57,576 --> 00:09:58,746
It's splitting.

206
00:09:58,796 --> 00:10:01,046
Buyers are going either
cheaper, electrified,

207
00:10:01,096 --> 00:10:04,566
or much bigger and the traditional
mid-range diesel dual-cab is getting

208
00:10:04,616 --> 00:10:06,116
squeezed from all sides.

209
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,971
BYD, meanwhile, is
turning up the pressure.

210
00:10:09,021 --> 00:10:13,611
From the 1st of October to
the 21st of December 2026,

211
00:10:13,661 --> 00:10:18,431
BYD is offering $4,000 cashback across
much of its range including the Shark

212
00:10:18,481 --> 00:10:19,141
6.

213
00:10:19,191 --> 00:10:25,251
CarsGuide listed the Shark 6
cab-chassis Dynamic at $51,990 before

214
00:10:25,301 --> 00:10:28,231
on-road costs with the cashback applied,

215
00:10:28,281 --> 00:10:33,351
the Premium at $53,900 and
the Performance at $62,900.

216
00:10:33,401 --> 00:10:36,771
Cars have to be delivered
by the 31st of December.

217
00:10:36,821 --> 00:10:40,071
And at the top end of the market,
the fight is just as fierce.

218
00:10:40,121 --> 00:10:46,596
In May 2026, Mitsubishi priced its new
Triton Raider at $74,990 drive-away.

219
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:51,724
CarExpert worked out that a Ford
Ranger Tremor came to about $82,404

220
00:10:51,774 --> 00:10:58,551
drive-away for a private buyer in
Sydney, and a HiLux Rugged X to $78,117.

221
00:10:58,601 --> 00:11:02,171
That's several thousand dollars of
difference between three utes that do very

222
00:11:02,221 --> 00:11:03,171
similar jobs.

223
00:11:03,221 --> 00:11:05,551
GWM has played the same game.

224
00:11:05,601 --> 00:11:10,531
In 2025 it cut its Cannon Alpha
plug-in hybrid by up to $7,100,

225
00:11:10,581 --> 00:11:14,551
to $57,490 drive-away.

226
00:11:14,601 --> 00:11:17,911
Every brand is chasing the same
shrinking pool of buyers and the easiest

227
00:11:17,961 --> 00:11:19,251
weapon is price.

228
00:11:19,301 --> 00:11:20,331
And there's more coming.

229
00:11:20,381 --> 00:11:24,101
The JAC Hunter plug-in hybrid has been
targeting less than fifty thousand

230
00:11:24,151 --> 00:11:24,894
dollars drive-away.

231
00:11:24,944 --> 00:11:29,411
Chery has a diesel-electric
ute due before the end of 2026.

232
00:11:29,461 --> 00:11:33,031
GWM plans a plug-in hybrid
version of its smaller Cannon.

233
00:11:33,081 --> 00:11:37,731
And Nissan's next Navara is set to use
Mitsubishi's plug-in hybrid technology.

234
00:11:37,781 --> 00:11:41,101
More choice means more competition
and more pressure on prices.

235
00:11:43,177 --> 00:11:45,900
Now here's the twist and it's why the
timing of your purchase matters so much.

236
00:11:45,950 --> 00:11:47,820
These discounts might not last.

237
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:52,680
In fact, Toyota itself has warned
that ute prices could go up in 2027.

238
00:11:52,730 --> 00:11:54,780
Under the New Vehicle Efficiency Standard,

239
00:11:54,830 --> 00:11:59,620
the emissions target for utes and vans
is 180 grams of CO2 per kilometre in

240
00:11:59,670 --> 00:12:01,080
2026.

241
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:03,920
In 2027, it drops to 150.

242
00:12:03,970 --> 00:12:09,160
CarsGuide reported the HiLux SR5 with
Toyota's mild-hybrid diesel is claimed

243
00:12:09,210 --> 00:12:14,040
at 191 grams per kilometre
already above the 2026 limit,

244
00:12:14,090 --> 00:12:16,800
and 41 grams over the 2027 one.

245
00:12:16,850 --> 00:12:20,920
Toyota's John Pappas has called the 2027
targets for light commercial vehicles

246
00:12:20,970 --> 00:12:22,280
"really challenging".

247
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:25,260
And Toyota said it "cannot
rule out" price increases.

248
00:12:25,310 --> 00:12:30,460
That's a warning, not a price list nobody
has announced a 2027 price rise yet.

249
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:32,160
And the first actual penalty bills,

250
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:34,080
for vehicles sold in 2025,

251
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:37,440
aren't due to be determined
until February 2028,

252
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:39,760
so car makers still have
time to trade credits.

253
00:12:39,810 --> 00:12:42,660
But it tells you which way
the pressure is pushing.

254
00:12:42,710 --> 00:12:44,500
There's another possibility too.

255
00:12:44,550 --> 00:12:47,160
On the 29th of September 2026,

256
00:12:47,210 --> 00:12:51,180
the federal Coalition pledged to
repeal the NVES if it wins government,

257
00:12:51,230 --> 00:12:53,380
calling it a "family car and ute tax".

258
00:12:53,430 --> 00:12:55,560
So the rules themselves could change.

259
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:56,840
The point is simple:

260
00:12:56,890 --> 00:12:59,720
the conditions creating
today's deals are unusual,

261
00:12:59,770 --> 00:13:01,530
and they might not be here in a year.

262
00:13:02,303 --> 00:13:05,123
So how do you get the best deal
in the middle of a ute price war?

263
00:13:05,173 --> 00:13:08,313
First, compare drive-away
prices, not headlines.

264
00:13:08,363 --> 00:13:13,533
A "$4,000 bonus" and a "$4,000 fuel
card" aren't the same as $4,000 off the

265
00:13:13,583 --> 00:13:14,353
price.

266
00:13:14,403 --> 00:13:16,673
Ask every dealer for a
written drive-away price,

267
00:13:16,723 --> 00:13:19,053
including all accessories
you actually need.

268
00:13:19,103 --> 00:13:21,113
Second, read the finance conditions.

269
00:13:21,163 --> 00:13:24,693
The HiLux bonus requires Toyota
Finance and a minimum amount borrowed.

270
00:13:24,743 --> 00:13:28,273
That can still be a good deal but compare
the interest rate and the total cost

271
00:13:28,323 --> 00:13:29,373
of the loan with your bank.

272
00:13:29,423 --> 00:13:33,003
A bonus that's swallowed by
a higher rate isn't a bonus.

273
00:13:33,053 --> 00:13:36,233
Third, check the build date
and look at demonstrators.

274
00:13:36,283 --> 00:13:39,953
Toyota's offer covers demonstrators,
and many brands have runout stock.

275
00:13:40,003 --> 00:13:42,183
Older build dates should
mean a sharper price.

276
00:13:42,233 --> 00:13:44,233
Fourth, think about resale.

277
00:13:44,283 --> 00:13:47,453
Toyota and Ford utes have historically
held their value strongly.

278
00:13:47,503 --> 00:13:51,073
A heavily discounted ute from a brand
with weaker resale might cost you more

279
00:13:51,123 --> 00:13:52,153
when you sell.

280
00:13:52,203 --> 00:13:54,353
Look at the total cost over
the years you'll keep it,

281
00:13:54,403 --> 00:13:56,213
not just the price on day one.

282
00:13:56,263 --> 00:13:57,373
Fifth, use the calendar.

283
00:13:57,423 --> 00:14:00,693
Black Friday falls on
the 27th of November,

284
00:14:00,743 --> 00:14:03,433
BYD's cashback runs to
the 21st of December,

285
00:14:03,483 --> 00:14:06,953
and the HiLux finance window
closes on the 31st of December.

286
00:14:07,003 --> 00:14:10,233
Dealers chasing end-of-year targets
are often at their most flexible in the

287
00:14:10,283 --> 00:14:11,553
final weeks of December.

288
00:14:11,603 --> 00:14:14,113
And finally, buy the
ute you actually need.

289
00:14:14,163 --> 00:14:16,313
If you tow a heavy caravan every weekend,

290
00:14:16,363 --> 00:14:19,733
a cheap plug-in hybrid with a lower
towing capacity might not suit you,

291
00:14:19,783 --> 00:14:21,153
however good the deal.

292
00:14:21,203 --> 00:14:23,073
If you mostly drive in the suburbs,

293
00:14:23,123 --> 00:14:25,233
ask yourself whether
you need a ute at all.

294
00:14:25,283 --> 00:14:26,753
So should you buy now, or wait?

295
00:14:26,803 --> 00:14:28,973
If you need a ute in the next few months,

296
00:14:29,023 --> 00:14:31,773
this is one of the strongest
buyer's markets in years.

297
00:14:31,823 --> 00:14:36,913
Toyota, Ford, Kia and BYD are all
chasing volume before the end of 2026,

298
00:14:36,963 --> 00:14:39,093
and some of these deals end in December.

299
00:14:39,143 --> 00:14:42,133
But if you can wait, keep an eye on 2027.

300
00:14:42,183 --> 00:14:44,413
New plug-in and electric
utes are arriving,

301
00:14:44,463 --> 00:14:48,453
and if the emissions rules push prices
up, the deals could dry up quickly.

302
00:14:48,503 --> 00:14:51,833
Nobody can promise which way prices
will go but you'll be in a much stronger

303
00:14:51,883 --> 00:14:54,783
position if you know the numbers
before you walk into a dealership.

304
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:58,230
So, are ute prices
collapsing in Australia?

305
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:02,090
Not across the board but the discounting
is the biggest we've seen in years,

306
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:04,090
and it's coming from the very top.

307
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:07,030
Toyota is offering $4,000 on the HiLux.

308
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:10,150
Ford cut the Ranger Hybrid by
more than ten thousand dollars.

309
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,750
Kia slashed up to fifteen
thousand off the Tasman.

310
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:17,050
And BYD is throwing $4,000
cashback at the Shark 6.

311
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:18,430
The reason is simple:

312
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,710
Australians are buying
fewer traditional utes,

313
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,910
and every brand is fighting
over the buyers who are left.

314
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:26,610
For you, that means bargaining
power at least for now.

315
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,170
Here's what to watch next.

316
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:30,990
The October sales figures
land in early November,

317
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:33,870
and they'll show whether
Toyota's HiLux bonus is working.

318
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:38,010
The race between the Ranger and the
HiLux for the 2026 crown will go down to

319
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:38,910
the wire.

320
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:42,930
Black Friday and the end-of-year sales
push will bring another wave of deals.

321
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:44,370
And in 2027,

322
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:48,150
tougher emissions targets and a flood
of new plug-in utes will shake things up

323
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:48,930
all over again.

324
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:50,450
Whatever you drive,

325
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:54,050
the next six months could be one of the
best windows in a decade to negotiate

326
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:55,330
on a ute.

327
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:57,650
If this helped, hit like, subscribe,

328
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,830
and share it with a mate
who's shopping for a ute.

329
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,730
Tell me in the comments: Ranger,
HiLux, Shark or something else?

330
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:04,750
And in the next video,

331
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:08,410
we're looking at the new road tax that
could hit every driver in Australia not

332
00:16:08,460 --> 00:16:09,710
just EV owners.

333
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:10,560
See you there.
